<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bocchus I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 110–80 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bocchus I was king of Mauretania in north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and father-in-law of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a> of Numidia. He joined Jugurtha against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurthine-war">Jugurthine War</a>, but in 105 BCE betrayed him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Lucius Cornelius Sulla</a>, the quaestor of Marius, ending the war. Rome rewarded him with the western part of Numidia, and Sulla later showed the scene on his signet ring.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bocchus-i.jpg" alt="Bocchus I" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Bocchus_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
